        "quasi-stationary distribution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "bef-bes",
      "label": "BEF/BES: diversity-functioning/stability under environmental stochasticity (incl. meta-analysis work)",
      "keywords": [
        "biodiversity ecosystem functioning",
        "ecosystem stability",
        "asynchrony",
        "portfolio effect",
        "insurance hypothesis",
        "meta-analysis"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "forest-empirics",
      "label": "Forest-plot empirics: data-based tests of diversity, coexistence and stability",
      "keywords": [
        "ForestGEO",
        "boreal forest",
        "conspecific negative density dependence",
        "neighborhood competition",
        "tree species coexistence",
        "forest census"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "priority_questions": [
    "How do MCT mechanism partitions (storage effect / relative nonlinearity) generalise rigorously to multispecies and consumer-resource structures in stochastic environments?",
    "When do pairwise niche/fitness differences and structural (feasibility-domain) metrics agree or disagree in multispecies communities, and is there a principled community-level aggregation?",
    "How does environmental stochasticity (including autocorrelated noise and extreme events) jointly affect coexistence and BEF/BES relationships?",
    "Can permanence / invasion-graph theory yield coexistence criteria that are testable with real data?",
    "Which statistical models (IPMs, GLMM/GNLMM, hierarchical Bayesian) can reliably estimate the strength of coexistence mechanisms in boreal-forest and ForestGEO plots?"
  ],
